{#- Claude Code reads project hooks ONLY from settings files. A plain project's
    `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` is NOT a hook-config location — that path is valid
    for a PLUGIN bundle only (hooks.md's location table). Confirmed by controlled
    experiment 2026-07-17: the same commands fired from settings.json and not from
    `.claude/hooks/hooks.json`, in the same session and repo.

    ADR-006 staging (PLAN-permission-deny-and-hooks-wiring):
      Stage 1 (Phase 1) — non-blocking: telemetry, post_write_reminder,
        sessionid_envfile, autopilot_autoarm, flush_session.
      Stage 2 (Phase 2) — control-flow, **Stop event only**: loop_gate +
        autopilot_guard, both passing `--mode stop-hook` (the modules dispatch on
        it). loop_gate on Stop is what lets /hm:loop reach iteration 2. Stop-blocking
        is a materially lower risk class than tool-call blocking: it cannot block a
        tool call, it is bounded by each module's stop_hook_active guard, and the
        worst case is one extra turn.
      Stage 3 (Phase 3) — everything that can block an ORDINARY TOOL CALL:
        permission_gate, worktree_gate, spec_gate, **and autopilot_guard's PreToolUse
        copies**. They land last, with a live negative control, and atomically with
        ADR-007's `--subordinate-to-deny-dangerous` flag.

    The staging axis is the EVENT, not the module (REVIEW round 1, consensus P1 —
    codex + code-reviewer). A first draft put autopilot_guard wholesale in Stage 2
    because ADR-006 partitions by module name; but its PreToolUse path returns
    allow=False (autopilot_guard.py:330 → exit 2), so it satisfies BOTH conjuncts of
    ADR-006's own Stage-3 criterion — "can block ordinary tool calls AND has never
    executed in Claude Code" — and satisfies the second HARDER than permission_gate,
    which is at least live in Cursor and Codex. autopilot_guard is wired in NO IDE
    today. "Only blocks under autopilot" does not save it either: with
    `autonomy.autopilot_persistent: true`, autopilot_autoarm re-arms a marker at every
    SessionStart, so the block is unconditional for that population — and what they
    opted into was auto-advance, not "block my git push".

    Stage 3 is NOT wired here yet — there is deliberately no `PreToolUse` key. A first
    attempt was written and then REVERTED before landing: its review (Grade D) found two
    consensus P0s. The work is parked on branch `hm/phase34-parked`; see
    work-docs/REVIEW-permission-deny-and-hooks-wiring-phase34-2026-07-17.md before
    re-attempting. In short: (1) retiring `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` needs ADR-005's sweep
    exclusion + pristine-delete gate in the SAME commit, or reconcile deletes a hooks.json
    holding user-authored hooks; (2) `autopilot_guard`'s `permission-surface-write` rule
    needs a read-only ALLOWLIST, not a write-token blacklist — wiring PreToolUse is what
    makes that rule live, and a blacklist leaks (`python -c`, `perl -i`, `git checkout --`).
    When adding the groups, use matchers `Bash` and `Write|Edit|MultiEdit` byte-identical
    to hooks.json.j2:30,37. hooks.json.j2:44 renders spec_gate as `Write|Edit` (no
    MultiEdit) — that is a typo, not a contract; two groups may share a matcher (identity
    keys on matcher + EVERY command), so `Write|Edit|MultiEdit` does not collide.

    ADR-010: `sessionstart_drift` is deliberately absent — the plugin bundle
    (`hooks/hooks.json` at plugin root) already fires it; rendering it here too
    would double-register it for plugin users.

    Schema is Claude's: PascalCase event keys + nested {matcher?, hooks:[...]}.
    Cursor (.cursor/hooks.json) and Codex (.codex/hooks.json) own their own files
    with their own schemas — do NOT collapse them into this one.
-#}
{
  "permissions": {
    "allow": ["Read", "Bash(uv:*)", "Bash(pytest:*)", "Bash(git:*)"{% if config.second_opinion and 'codex' in config.second_opinion.models %}, "Bash(codex exec:*)"{% endif %}{% if config.second_opinion and 'antigravity' in config.second_opinion.models %}, "Bash(agy --print --sandbox:*)"{% endif %}],
    "deny": {% if config.permissions.deny_dangerous %}["Bash(rm:*)", "Bash(curl * | sh)", "Write(/etc/**)", "Write(~/.ssh/**)"]{% else %}[]{% endif %}
  },
  "hooks": {
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "*",
        "hooks": [
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.telemetry", "timeout": 5}
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.post_write_reminder", "timeout": 5}
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.loop_gate --mode stop-hook", "timeout": 10},
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.autopilot_guard --mode stop-hook", "timeout": 10}
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreCompact": [
      {
        "matcher": "auto",
        "hooks": [
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.flush_session", "timeout": 30, "statusMessage": "Snapshotting autoloop progress..."}
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "manual",
        "hooks": [
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.flush_session", "timeout": 30, "statusMessage": "Snapshotting autoloop progress..."}
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.sessionid_envfile"},
          {"type": "command", "command": "uv run --with '{{ harness_maker_src_path }}' python -m harness_maker.hooks.autopilot_autoarm"}
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "preset": "{{ preset }}"
}
